{
  "title": "How to make a thumb impression for exam forms",
  "description": "Make a clear left thumb impression for IBPS, SBI, NEET or DSSSB forms at home — ink, paper, pressing, scanning, and the exact KB and pixel size.",
  "lang": "en",
  "slug": "thumb-impression-for-exam-forms",
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z",
  "relatedExams": [
    "ibps-po",
    "sbi-clerk",
    "neet-ug",
    "dsssb",
    "htet",
    "iaf-agniveervayu"
  ],
  "relatedTools": [
    "thumb-impression",
    "compress-image",
    "resize-image"
  ],
  "order": 4,
  "draft": false,
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Banking forms (IBPS, SBI, RBI, NABARD), NEET, HTET, DSSSB and IAF Agniveervayu ask for a "
        },
        {
          "text": "thumb impression",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " upload. Most people have never made one at home. A smudged black blob is the usual result — and smudged impressions get rejected."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Here is how to make a clean one in about five minutes, and how to get it to the exact size your exam wants."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "What you need"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ul",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "A "
            },
            {
              "text": "stamp ink pad",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " (black or blue). Any stationery shop has one for about ₹30–50."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "A "
            },
            {
              "text": "plain white A4 sheet",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — printer paper, no lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Tissue or a cloth to wipe your thumb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Your phone, and daylight or a bright room light."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "No ink pad? A blue or black ballpoint refill rubbed on the thumb works in a pinch, but an ink pad gives a much cleaner print."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Which thumb?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Banking notices ask for the "
        },
        {
          "text": "left thumb",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". If you do not have a left thumb, they allow the right one — the rule is in the notice. NEET is different: it asks for "
        },
        {
          "text": "all fingers and thumbs of both hands",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". DSSSB asks for "
        },
        {
          "text": "left and right thumb as two separate files",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". Read your exam’s rules first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Step 1: Make the impression"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Wash and fully dry your hands. Oily skin smudges."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Press your thumb "
            },
            {
              "text": "lightly",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " on the ink pad. Dab two or three times — do not soak it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Check the thumb: the ridges should be inked, not a wet layer of ink."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Place the thumb flat on the paper and press down with gentle, firm pressure. Count to two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "For full coverage, roll the thumb "
            },
            {
              "text": "very slightly",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to each side — just enough to print the edges — without letting it slide. Then "
            },
            {
              "text": "lift straight up",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Sliding or a big roll is what causes smudges."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Make 3–4 impressions on the sheet, with space between them. You will pick the best one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Let the ink dry for a minute before you take the photo."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A good impression shows clear ridge lines across the whole thumb tip. If it is a solid dark patch, you used too much ink. If it is patchy and pale, use a bit more."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Step 2: Photograph it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ul",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Keep the paper flat on a table near a window."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Hold the phone directly above, parallel to the paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Turn flash "
            },
            {
              "text": "off",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and make sure no shadow falls on the print."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Get close enough that the impression fills a good part of the screen, then tap to focus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Take two or three shots and pick the sharpest."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "You do not need a scanner. A modern phone camera captures ridges well if the light is even."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Step 3: Crop, clean and resize"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Open "
        },
        {
          "text": "Thumb Impression",
          "href": "/tools/thumb-impression"
        },
        {
          "text": " on SahiSize, or go straight to your exam page."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Pick the photo",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — it stays on your phone; nothing is uploaded."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Crop",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " around one impression, leaving a small white margin. For banking the crop box is square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Clean",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — this makes the paper white and the ink darker, without filling in the ridges."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Fit to your exam",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — pixels and KB are set from the preset."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Check the ticks and download."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Thumb impression sizes for common exams"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Always check the latest official notice — these are from recent notices and can change between cycles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        [
          {
            "text": "Exam"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "Size"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "KB"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "Notes"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "IBPS PO",
              "href": "/exam/ibps-po"
            },
            {
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "text": "SBI Clerk",
              "href": "/exam/sbi-clerk"
            },
            {
              "text": ", RBI, NABARD"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "240 × 240 px (3 × 3 cm at 200 DPI)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "20–50 KB"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Left thumb, black or blue ink, white paper"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "NEET UG",
              "href": "/exam/neet-ug"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "KB only"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "50–200 KB"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "All fingers and thumbs, both hands"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "HTET",
              "href": "/exam/htet"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "KB only"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "10–50 KB"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Thumb impression"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "DSSSB",
              "href": "/exam/dsssb"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "KB only"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "up to 40 KB each"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Left and right thumb, separate files"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "IAF Agniveervayu",
              "href": "/exam/iaf-agniveervayu"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "KB only"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "50–100 KB"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Left thumb"
            }
          ]
        ],
        [
          [
            {
              "text": "SSC GD",
              "href": "/exam/ssc-gd"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Not in the notice"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Check the form"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Only if the online form asks for it"
            }
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A note on NEET: the bulletin mentions two ranges (10–200 KB in one place, 50–300 KB in another). SahiSize uses "
        },
        {
          "text": "50–200 KB",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", which satisfies both."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The NEET finger impressions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "For NEET you need all ten prints. The usual way is:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "On one A4 sheet, make the four fingers of the left hand in a row, then the left thumb next to them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Below that, do the same for the right hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Write “Left hand” and “Right hand” above each row in small letters, if the form or bulletin asks for labels."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Photograph the whole sheet in one shot, flat and sharp."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Check the NEET form for whether it wants one image or separate images per hand, as the layout has changed between years."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Common mistakes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "ul",
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Too much ink.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " The ridges fill in and the print becomes a blob. Dab lightly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Sliding or over-rolling the thumb.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " It smears the edges. Press flat, roll only slightly, and lift straight up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Lined paper or coloured paper.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Use plain white."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Shadow of the phone on the print.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Move the light or the phone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Photo of a photo.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Never photograph a print shown on another screen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Wrong hand.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Banking wants the left thumb unless you do not have one."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "FAQ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Can I use blue ink?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Yes for banking — the notice says black or blue. NEET also allows black or blue. Black usually comes out a little crisper after compression."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "My file is only 12 KB but IBPS wants 20–50 KB. What now?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A clean thumb print on white paper compresses very well. SahiSize’s preset raises quality and, if needed, adds invisible padding so the file reaches 20 KB without changing how it looks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Can I make the thumb impression with a mobile app or fingerprint sensor?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "No. Exams want an ink impression on paper. A phone fingerprint sensor does not produce an image you can upload."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Do I need the same thumb impression at the exam centre?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Biometric thumb or finger scans are often taken at the centre and during document verification. Your uploaded impression should be a genuine one of your own thumb."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Is SahiSize the official tool of any exam?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "No. SahiSize is independent and not linked to any exam body. Always check the latest official notice. Next, see the "
        },
        {
          "text": "handwritten declaration guide",
          "href": "/guides/handwritten-declaration-format"
        },
        {
          "text": " and the "
        },
        {
          "text": "signature scanning guide",
          "href": "/guides/scan-signature-with-phone"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
